const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文考察股票横截面中的波动差异与预期收益之间的经验关系。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“The Cross-Section of Volatility and Expected Returns” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2006.00818.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2006) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2006) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"研究按个股或组合的波动特征进行横截面比较，重点是排序、控制变量和后续收益的定义。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “The Cross-Section of Volatility and Expected Returns”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2006.00818.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2006) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2006) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"波动估计、股票范围、市值权重、断点和回报持有期必须一起保存，不能只保留最终分组标签。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “The Cross-Section of Volatility and Expected Returns”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2006.00818.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2006) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2006) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"横截面结果描述的是特定样本中的条件比较，而不是把波动作为单独足够的定价因子。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “The Cross-Section of Volatility and Expected Returns”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2006.00818.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2006) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2006) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"检查微盘股、退市、流动性、极端值处理和断点来源，并确保特征在投资期前已可观察。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “The Cross-Section of Volatility and Expected Returns”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2006.00818.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2006) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2006) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 The Journal of Finance (2006)。横截面关联不构成任何标的的风险判断，更不能绕过组合形成与执行成本。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites The Journal of Finance (2006) for “The Cross-Section of Volatility and Expected Returns”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.2006.00818.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2006) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2006) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“The Cross-Section of Volatility and Expected Returns”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。横截面关联不构成任何标的的风险判断，更不能绕过组合形成与执行成本。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “The Cross-Section of Volatility and Expected Returns”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
